## Validation

- [ ] Every referenced asset/reference/script exists.
- [ ] Every claimed capability has implementation backing.
- [ ] The full package structure is present.
- [ ] Relevant implementation and tests were actually executed.
- [ ] The skill is invokable as `/pmcro-skills:<skill-name>`.
- [ ] All examples and agent handoffs use the namespaced selector.

## Implementation Gate

Before exposing a capability:

1. Confirm the implementation exists.
2. Run it against a safe fixture or scratch target.
3. Confirm the documented output matches observed behavior.
4. If implementation is missing, implement it before using or documenting the capability.

## Completion Rule

Structure alone is not sufficient. A skill is complete only after its declared implementation has been executed and its output verified.

The generated package should include an executable `scripts/validate-skill.ps1` derived from the validator template.
